```
@Transactional
public PollinationOperation pollinate(...) {
    String hash = hash(...);
    var existing = opRepo.findByRequestId(requestId);
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        var op = existing.get();
        if (!op.requestHash().equals(hash)) throw conflict("REQUEST_ID_MISMATCH", ...);
        return op;
    }
    Inflorescence inf = inflRepo.findById(id).orElseThrow(notFound);
    if (inf.removedAt() != null) throw unprocessable INFLORESCENCE_REMOVED;
    PollinationWindow w = inf.window();
    if (executedAt.isBefore(w.openAt())) throw unprocessable WINDOW_NOT_STARTED;
    if (!w.contains(executedAt)) throw unprocessable WINDOW_EXPIRED;
    PollenBatch batch = batchRepo.findByBatchNo(pollenBatchNo).orElseThrow(unprocessable BATCH_NOT_FOUND);
    if (batch.status() == DISABLED) throw unprocessable BATCH_DISABLED;
    long opId = opRepo.insert(...);  // may throw DuplicateKey → translate
    if (inflRepo.occupyIfFree(id, opId) == 0) throw conflict ACTIVE_OPERATION_EXISTS;
    return opRepo.findById(opId).get();
}
```
On conflict exception, transaction rolls back the insert. Good.

DuplicateKeyException on insert → catch and translate: find by requestId; if hash matches return it; else conflict. But careful: if DuplicateKey thrown, in H2 the transaction may be marked rollback-only? With Spring + DataSourceTransactionManager, the connection is fine; H2 doesn't abort the transaction on constraint violation (unlike Postgres). So catch-and-continue works on H2 and MySQL. OK.

revoke:
```
@Transactional
public PollinationOperation revoke(long operationId, Instant revokedAt) {
    PollinationOperation op = opRepo.findById(operationId).orElseThrow(notFound);
    if (op.status() == REVOKED) return op; // 幂等
    if (op.status() == CONFIRMED) throw unprocessable OPERATION_CONFIRMED;
    if (opRepo.revokeIfEffective(operationId, revokedAt) == 0) {
        // 竞争失败：确认已抢先
        throw conflict TERMINAL_RACE;
    }
    inflRepo.releaseIfHeldBy(op.inflorescenceId(), operationId);
    return opRepo.findById(operationId).get();
}
```

